var tafsirData_77 = {
  "1": "\"By those ˹winds˺ sent forth successively,\" opens Surah al-Mursalat with winds, the first of several oaths. The winds are signs and agents.\n\n“By those winds sent forth successively” translates “wa al-mursalati ‘urfa,” by those sent, successive, like the winds sent forth, rainclouds scattered widely, angels distinguishing, delivering revelation, and winds blowing violently. Mursalati ‘urfa is winds sent in succession, like the revelation revealed in stages to you O Prophet and the reminders sent to bring from darkness. The winds are the same that were furious, bitter for ‘Ad seven nights and eight days, that delight planters with rain then wither to chaff, and that the garden owners’ harvest depended on.\n\nThis oath follows the grateful vs ungrateful division and the reminder that whoever wills may take the Right Way, showing that winds are part of the reminder to humankind, a warning as Hell is warning.\n\nSuccession indicates order, like the Pen and what everyone writes in order, the seven heavens one above another, and the earth and mountains crushed with one blow.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to worship winds. Winds are created, sent by the Lord of east and west, no god except Him, take Him as Trustee.\n\nFor the living who are told to take the Right Way and recite what is easy, winds sent forth successively should move you to be mindful to best ability, hear and obey, spend, and be saved from selfishness, so winds become your abundant rain to drink, not the furious wind that destroyed ‘Ad, and your vast kingdom’s bliss remains, not the raging Flame that summons hoarders who gathered and hoarded.\n\nExtra: Winds sent forth successively also recall the winds that the garden owners’ harvest depended on, the rain that delights planters then withers to chaff, and the furious bitter wind that destroyed ‘Ad for seven nights and eight days. Succession shows order, like the Pen and what everyone writes successively, the seven heavens one above another, and the Reminder revealed in stages. The winds’ succession is the same order that makes the garden’s ashes while they slept and the earth and mountains crushed with one blow, showing the Most Capable’s Hands hold authority. To be among the grateful, let successive winds remind you to be mindful to best ability, hear and obey, spend, and be saved from selfishness, so winds become abundant rain to drink, not furious wind.",
  "2": "\"and those blowing violently,\" continues the winds oath after sent forth successively. The violence shows power.\n\n“and those blowing violently” translates “fa-al-‘asifati ‘asfa,” the violent storm winds, as with the furious, bitter wind that destroyed ‘Ad, the torment that struck the garden while they slept, and the earth and mountains shaking violently, reduced to dunes. Blowing violently indicates the winds’ force that delights planters when gentle rain then withers, and that the disobedient feel secure One in heaven will not unleash stones, yet this wind is unleashed by the Most Capable who holds all authority.\n\nThis follows sent forth successively to show that winds are both successive and violent, gentle for mercy and violent for punishment, like the rain that could be made salty, the harvest that could be chaff, and the Day that is easy for Allah.\n\nViolent blowing is also the Pen’s close, the Trumpet’s one blast, the Inevitable’s one crushing.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear violent winds as merely destructive. Violent winds also scatter rainclouds widely, as next, bringing abundant rain to those who seek forgiveness.\n\nFor the covered who is told to arise and warn, violent winds blown are a sign to warn with, revering your Lord, purifying garments, shunning idols, so violent becomes the warning to humankind, to whichever chooses to take the lead or lag, and you choose the lead, among the people of the right in Gardens asking about the wicked, not among the spooked zebras fleeing from the reminder as from a lion.\n\nMore: Blowing violently also recalls the swallowing earth as it quakes violently and mountains reduced to dunes, the sky split apart, and the Trumpet’s difficult Day. Violent blowing is the Pen’s close, the Inevitable’s crushing, the Fire that almost bursts. Violent is also the distress when touched with evil that makes halu‘ distressed. The violence now is a sign, not yet the Day’s violence, giving a little while to bear with deniers, leave them to Him who has shackles, and to be patient with decree. Let violent remind you to be among those in awe without seeing, whose mighty reward is forgiveness, so violent becomes the scattering of rainclouds widely for provision, not the wind that leaves you like uprooted palm trunks.",
  "3": "\"and those scattering ˹rainclouds˺ widely!\" completes the winds trio after sent forth and blowing violently. Scattering is distribution.\n\n“and those scattering rainclouds widely!” translates “wa al-nashirati nashra,” those that spread and scatter, dispersing clouds, as with the abundant rain showered after seeking forgiveness, the gardens and rivers supplied, and the rain that delights planters then becomes chaff, and the water that if it were to sink who could bring flowing water.\n\nScattering widely, or “nashra,” is to spread, like the earth spread for spacious pathways to walk, the Pen spreading what everyone writes, and the reminder spread to the whole world.\n\nWinds scattering rainclouds bring the abundant rain to drink as a test, had the deniers followed Right Way, We would have granted abundant rain, but they turned from remembrance into overwhelming punishment.\n\nThis follows blowing violently to show that violent becomes scattering, punishment becomes provision, as with the weighty revelation soon sent that is heavy but made light through night impact.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to separate scattering from distinguishing. Winds scattering is physical, but next, angels distinguishing truth from falsehood, shows physical and spiritual scattering both.\n\nFor the human created from mixed drop to test, shown the Way grateful or ungrateful, winds scattering widely should make you grateful, fulfilling vows, feeding despite desire, so scattering becomes your Gardens’ rivers under which rivers flow for ever and ever, not the Fire’s chains, shackles, and blazing Fire prepared for the ungrateful, and your vast kingdom’s bliss is scattered widely in Gardens held in honour.\n\nFurther: Scattering rainclouds widely also shows the Most Compassionate who holds birds and smooths earth for you to move, the Lord of east and west capable to replace, and the Treasuries belonging to Allah. Scattering is provision, like gardens and rivers supplied after seeking forgiveness, the spring flowing at will, and the Gardens under rivers for ever and ever. Widely indicates abundance, opposite to hoarded wealth gathered that the Flame summons. To be grateful, let scattering remind you to fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, give food despite desire, so scattering becomes your bliss and vast kingdom, where fruit is made very easy to reach and silver vessels are precisely filled.",
  "4": "\"And ˹by˺ those ˹angels˺ fully distinguishing ˹truth from falsehood˺,\" shifts the oath from winds to angels after sent, violent, scattering. Distinguishing is the angels’ role.\n\n“And by those angels fully distinguishing truth from falsehood” translates “fa-al-fariqati farqa,” the separators who separate, as with the Balance so people may administer justice, the Light that brings from darkness, the Reminder that would humble a mountain, and the Pen that distinguishes what is written. Distinguishing follows scattering, as winds scatter clouds, angels distinguish truth.\n\nFully, or farqa, indicates complete separation, as with submitted not wicked, Gardens vs raging Flame, bright vs gloomy, detained every soul except people of the right, and the wall with gate between grace and torment.\n\nAngels distinguishing are also like stern guards with shooting stars that distinguish eavesdropping devils, and the nineteen wardens that test.\n\nThis follows winds to show that natural signs and angelic acts both guide.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat distinguishing as human judgment that equates submitted and wicked, asking “Should We treat submitted like wicked? What is the matter with you?” Angelic distinguishing is flawless, unlike despicable oath-taker, slanderer, gossip-monger.\n\nFor the living who were nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful, let the angels’ distinguishing teach you to distinguish, to take the Right Way, recite what is easy, establish prayer, pay alms, lend good loan, and seek forgiveness, so distinguishing becomes your Gardens held in honour where you are told to eat and drink joyfully for what you did in days gone by, not the raging Flame that rips scalps.\n\nExtra: Fully distinguishing truth from falsehood also parallels the Balance so people may administer justice, the Light that brings from darkness, and the Reminder that would humble a mountain. Angels fully distinguishing is flawless, unlike despicable’s distinguishing that slanders, withholds, and says ancient fables. Fully indicates complete separation, as with submitted not wicked, detained every soul except people of the right, and the wall with gate. For the human created from mixed drop, shown the Way grateful or ungrateful, letting angels distinguish teaches you to distinguish, to take the Right Way, recite what is easy, establish prayer, pay alms, lend good loan, and seek forgiveness, so distinguishing becomes your Gardens held in honour, not the deviant fuel for Hell.",
  "5": "\"and those delivering revelation,\" adds the fifth oath, the angels who deliver revelation, after distinguishing truth from falsehood. Delivery is central.\n\n“and those delivering revelation” translates “fa-al-mulqiyati dhikra,” the casters of reminder, as with the revelation revealed in stages to you O Prophet, the weighty revelation soon sent, the Reminder for the whole world, the Light, the Pen, and the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance so we believed. Delivering revelation is what the noble Messenger does as recitation not poet or fortune-teller but revelation from Lord of all worlds, guarded before and behind by angel-guards to ensure messengers fully deliver, though He already knows and keeps account of everything.\n\nThis follows distinguishing to show that after separating truth, the angels deliver it.\n\nDelivering revelation is the same as the jinn’s “We have heard an amazing recitation, it leads to Right Guidance.”\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear delivering as mere transmission without impact, like worthless planks leaned. Delivering is impactful, suitable for recitation at night, more forceful in treading.\n\nFor practice, receive the delivered revelation as the jinn did, readily believe, have no fear of being wronged, submit and seek right course, not deviant fuel for Hell, so delivered becomes your vast kingdom and bliss, where you are waited on with silver vessels and crystal, ginger and Salsabil, eternal youths, and pure drink, where striving is appreciated.\n\nMore: Delivering revelation also is the noble Messenger’s recitation not poet or fortune-teller, but revelation from Lord of all worlds, guarded before and behind by angel-guards to ensure delivery though He already knows and keeps account. Delivering is the Pen and what everyone writes, the well-preserved Record only purified touch, and the Ark as reminder for attentive ears. The angels delivering to the Messenger parallel the winds delivering rain, both mercy. To receive delivering, be like the jinn who said “We have heard an amazing recitation, it leads to Right Guidance so we believed and will never associate,” so delivered becomes your right course sought, your bliss and vast kingdom, and your pure drink from the Lord.",
  "6": "\"ending excuses and giving warnings.\" defines the purpose of delivering revelation, after the five oaths. The angels deliver to end excuses and warn.\n\n“ending excuses and giving warnings” translates “‘udhran aw nudhra,” as excuse or warning, as with “So the pleas of intercessors will be of no benefit to them” because excuses after the inevitable came are not accepted, “Make no excuses this Day, you are only rewarded for what you used to do,” and the keepers asking “Did a warner not come?” Excuses, or “‘udhran,” are justifications, as with “despite the excuses they come up with, the soul is a witness against itself,” and giving warnings, or “nudhran,” is the same as arise and warn, warn your people before painful punishment, and Hell as warning to humankind.\n\nEnding excuses means that delivering revelation removes the plea “We were not of those who heard,” as with attentive ears that grasp the Ark reminder, and giving warnings means that the mighty catastrophe, raging Flame, dunes, choking food are warned.\n\nThis follows delivering revelation to show that delivery has two effects, cutting excuses and providing warning, similar to the garden reduced to ashes while they slept that ended excuses for withholding.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think ending excuses is harsh. It is mercy that makes the soul’s testimony against itself clear now, before the Day it will be informed of what was sent forth and left behind.\n\nFor the human created from mixed drop, shown the Way, grateful or ungrateful, the delivered revelation ends your excuses now, so you cannot say on the Day “Had we listened and reasoned, we would not be among residents of Blaze,” but you did listen and reason, protected families, walked upright, and became among those in Gardens held in honour, whose excuses are not needed because their striving has been appreciated and they are told “All this is surely a reward for you.”",
  "7": "\"Surely, what you are promised will come to pass.\" confirms the oaths that preceded, the winds sent, blowing, scattering, angels distinguishing and delivering to end excuses and give warnings. The promise is the Day of Decision.\n\n“Surely, what you are promised will come to pass” translates the answer to “When is the Day of Judgment?” and “When will this threat come?” The promised includes the Day of Decision, the Day fifty thousand years, the difficult Day far from easy, the Inevitable that will have come to pass when Trumpet is blown, earth and mountains crushed, sky torn, Throne borne, presentation with no secrets hidden, bright and gloomy faces, collar bones, feet tied, driven to your Lord. Will come to pass indicates certainty, as with the garden reduced to ashes while they slept, the blast for Thamud, wind for ‘Ad, stern grip for Pharaoh, and the appointed time that never delays.\n\nSurely, or emphatic, shows the oath by winds and angels is not poetry, but guarantee, as with the Pen, the mountain-humbling Reminder, and the absolute truth.\n\nThis follows ending excuses and giving warnings to show what is promised.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear promised as distant, like they see it as far but We see it as near.\n\nFor the wrapped who stands at night reciting properly, what you are promised will come to pass is the Gardens held in honour where you are told to eat and drink joyfully, not the raging Flame that rips scalps. To ensure it comes to pass as Gardens for you, be among the grateful who fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, give food despite desire, and fear the distressful Day, so promise becomes your radiance and joy, Garden and silk.\n\nExtra: What you are promised also includes the Gardens for the virtuous with camphor drink, spring flowing at will, radiance, joy, Garden and silk, and the blazing Fire for the ungrateful. Promised will come to pass distinguishes the two, as with residents of Fire not equal residents of Paradise. The promise is not the powerless force that would help instead of the Most Compassionate, nor the honour that expels inferior, nor merchandise better than what is with Allah. It is the Pen’s promise, the Mountain’s humbling, the Ark’s reminder, and the Trustee’s will. To have it come to pass as Gardens for you, be grateful, fulfil vows, fear the sweeping horror, give food despite desire, and fear the distressful Day, so promised becomes radiance and Gardens held in honour.",
  "8": "\"So when the stars are put out,\" begins the description of what will come to pass, the Day of Decision’s cosmic signs. The first sign is stellar extinction.\n\n“So when the stars are put out” translates “fa-idha al-nujumu tumisat,” when stars are effaced, dimmed, obliterated, as with stars put out, sky torn apart, mountains blown away, and messengers’ time comes. Stars put out contrasts with the lowest heaven adorned with lamps as missiles against devils and the moon and sun placed within seven heavens. Stars that were lamps become dark, like the moon dimmed and sun and moon brought together, and the sky like molten brass and wool mountains.\n\nWhen indicates the appointed time that never delays, the Day they indulged until they faced, the Trumpet’s one blast. The stars’ putting out is the same as stars falling, the Pen’s writing that heavens are without flaw now fails as flawless becomes frail.\n\nThis follows what you are promised will come to pass to detail its signs.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat stars put out as ordinary night. It is the Inevitable’s extinguishing, far worse than chaff and ashes.\n\nFor the human created from humble fluid placed in secure place until appointed time, stars put out should humble, as with looking again at flawless heavens without finding flaw, now seeing stars put out. Be in awe without seeing, whose mighty reward is forgiveness, so stars put out is not your gloom but your confirmation that the promise will come to pass as Gardens where lamps are not needed because light is perfected and your face is bright looking at your Lord.\n\nMore: Stars put out also inverts the lowest heaven adorned with lamps as missiles against devils, the moon as reflected light and sun as radiant lamp within seven heavens. Stars that were lamps become dark, like the moon dimmed and sun and moon brought together, and the sky like molten brass, mountains like wool. Putting out is the opposite of adorning, showing the same Hands that adorn can extinguish, the Most Capable who holds all authority. For the grateful who give rightful share, stars put out is not your darkness but your confirmation that the promise will come to pass as vast kingdom and bliss, where no stars are needed because light is perfected and your face is bright looking at your Lord.",
  "9": "\"and the sky is torn apart,\" gives the second cosmic sign after stars put out. The sky, previously flawless, is ruptured.\n\n“and the sky is torn apart” translates “wa idha al-sama’u furijat,” when heaven is cleft, split, as with the sky will then be so torn that it will be frail with angels on its sides and eight bearing the Throne, the sky like molten brass, and the sky will even cause children’s hair to turn grey, His promise must be fulfilled. Torn apart contrasts with seven heavens one above another without flaw where sight returns frustrated, and the lowest heaven adorned with lamps.\n\nSky torn is the same as the Inevitable’s sky torn, the Trumpet’s sky torn, showing the same Day of Decision.\n\nWhen indicates the appointed time, the Day of mutual loss and gain, the Day you will be presented with no secret hidden.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think sky torn is repairable, like dunes of shifting sand that could be rebuilt. Torn sky is unrepairable in its worldly form, but will be replaced, as with replacing with others better and cannot be prevented.\n\nFor the living who love fleeting and neglect the weighty Day, sky torn should be heavier than fleeting. Let it move you to take the Right Way, recite what is easy, establish prayer, pay alms, lend good loan, and seek forgiveness, so sky torn is not your horror but the opening to the Throne borne by eight, where your presentation is with light ahead and you are among the bright faces, not gloomy anticipating devastation.\n\nFurther: Sky torn apart also recalls the Day earth and mountains will be lifted and crushed, dunes of shifting sand, children’s hair grey, and theInevitablesky torn frail with angels on sides and Throne borne by eight. Torn is cleft, as with the Inevitable’s sky torn, showing the flawless seven heavens you looked at without finding flaw now frail at divine command, not flaw. The sky that was adorned now tears to reveal the Throne, so the reminder to take the Right Way is urgent. For the wrapped who stands half the night reciting properly, sky torn is not horror but opening, where the Day fifty thousand years becomes your Gardens held in honour, not the raging Flame.",
  "10": "\"and the mountains are blown away,\" gives the third cosmic sign after stars and sky. Mountains, the firmest, are dispersed.\n\n“and the mountains are blown away” translates “wa idha al-jibalu nusifat,” when mountains are scattered as dust, blown, as with the Inevitable Event that will debase and elevate, earth shaken violently and mountains crushed to scattered dust, earth and mountains lifted and crushed with one blow, dunes of shifting sand on the Day earth and mountains shake, and mountains like tufts of wool. Blown away indicates pulverized, like tufts, like dunes, like palm trunks uprooted for ‘Ad.\n\nMountains blown away follows sky torn to show earth and heavens both undone, as with the garden reduced to ashes while they slept, but on cosmic scale.\n\nWhen indicates the Day of Decision, the promised will come to pass.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think mountains blown away is mere landslide, manageable by the Lord of pathways. It is total, showing no stronghold puts you out of reach.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid, mountains blown away humbles the despicable withholder who thought wealth and children prove ancient fables and the luxury deniers who indulge until they face their Day. To avoid being blown away with them, be among the requested to give food despite desire, whose Garden’s shade is right above and fruit easy, whose mountains remain as honour in Gardens held in honour where you never see scorching heat or bitter cold.\n\nAdditional: Mountains blown away also fulfills the Inevitable’s scattered particles of dust, earth and mountains lifted and crushed with one blow, and the garden reduced to ashes while they slept. Blown away, or “nusifat,” is to be scattered like tufts of wool, dunes, and palm trunks uprooted for ‘Ad. Blown away shows no stronghold puts you out of reach, no wealth and children divert, and no honour expels inferior can keep. For the virtuous who were nothing, drop, test, Way shown, grateful, the mountains blown away is the removal of barriers to the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, where scattered becomes gathered in Gardens held in honour, and the difficult Day far from easy becomes easy for the persevering.",
  "11": "\"and the messengers’ time ˹to testify˺ comes up—\" adds the human, prophetic sign after cosmic signs. The messengers’ appointed time arrives.\n\n“and the messengers’ time to testify comes up—” translates “wa idha al-rusulu uqqitat,” when messengers are appointed a time, set for a term. Time to testify, or “uqqitat,” is to be scheduled for testimony, like the Day of Decision set for which Day has all this been set, and like the appointed time until which humble fluid is placed in a secure place. Messengers’ time is when they will testify that they delivered, as with the jinn’s amazing recitation delivered, the Ark as reminder, and the keepers asking “Did a warner not come?”\n\nThis follows mountains blown away to show that after cosmos undone, humanity’s witnesses are summoned, as with the presentation where no secret stays hidden and the Throne borne by eight.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think messengers’ time is to be judged as deniers. Messengers are witnesses, not on trial like the despicable who said ancient fables.\n\nFor the living, the messengers’ time to testify should make you hear the messenger now, the illiterate messenger reciting, purifying, teaching, and Noah warning day and night, openly and privately, so your testimony is “I surely knew I would face my reckoning” in a life of bliss, not “I wish I had not been given my record” and woe and more woe.\n\nMore: Messengers’ time to testify also parallels the jinn’s hearing of amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance so we believed, and the Ark as reminder for attentive ears, and the keepers asking “Did a warner not come?” on each cast into the Fire that almost bursts. Messengers’ time is the scheduled testimony, as with the Day of Decision set, the appointed time until which humble fluid is in a secure place, and the Day every soul detained except the people of the right. To be among the testified for, hear the messenger now, the illiterate messenger reciting, purifying, teaching, whose outstanding character and never-ending reward prove sanity, not madness, so testimony is “Read my record, I knew I would face my reckoning,” not “I wish I had not been given my record.”",
  "12": "\"for which Day has all this been set?\" asks after listing stars put out, sky torn, mountains blown, messengers timed. The question heightens anticipation.\n\n“for which Day has all this been set?” translates “li-ayyi yawmin ujjilat,” for which Day has it been postponed, set? Set, or “ujjilat,” is to be deferred to a term, as with the appointed time that can never be delayed when it comes, the Day they indulged until they faced, the Day fifty thousand years, the appointed time until which the humble fluid stays in the secure place, and the Day every soul will be detained except the people of the right. The question echoes “What is the Inevitable Hour? What will make you realize what the Inevitable is?” after describing Thamud and ‘Ad, showing that the answer is weighty and needs prophetic informing.\n\nFor which Day indicates that stars, sky, mountains, and messengers all converge on one Day, not many, the same Day promised will come to pass.\n\nThis follows messengers’ time to show that their timing is for that Day.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to answer “for which Day” with speculation, as with “When will this threat come if you are truthful?” The Quran answers next, for the Day of Final Decision.\n\nFor practice, let “for which Day” make you take the Right Way while you will, recite what is easy, and be among those in awe without seeing, whose mighty reward is forgiveness, so the Day set is for you the elevated Garden where you are told to eat and drink joyfully, not the raging Flame that summons hoarders.\n\nExtra: For which Day has all this been set also echoes “What will make you realize what the Inevitable, what Hell is?” after describing Thamud and ‘Ad, showing that the Day set is weighty and needs informing. Set, or “ujjilat,” is to be postponed to a term, as with the appointed time that can never be delayed, the Day they indulged until they faced, the Day fifty thousand years, and the appointed time for humble fluid in secure place until We perfectly ordained. The Day set is the Day of Final Decision, the same as the Day of Decision, where stars put out, sky torn, mountains blown, messengers testify. To prepare, let “for which Day” make you take the Right Way while you will, recite what is easy, and be among the mindful whose light shines ahead.",
  "13": "\"For the Day of ˹Final˺ Decision!\" answers “for which Day has all this been set?” The Day is the criterion.\n\n“For the Day of Final Decision!” translates “li-yawmi al-fasl,” for the Day of Separation, Decision, as with the Day of Gathering for mutual loss and gain, the Day the disbelievers asked “When will this threat come?” and were told knowledge is with Allah, the Day children’s hair turns grey, and the Inevitable that will have come to pass. Final Decision, or “fasl,” is to distinguish truth from falsehood fully, as with angels distinguishing and delivering to end excuses and give warnings.\n\nDay of Final Decision is the same as the Day of Decision that will be asked “What will make you realize what the Day of Decision is? Woe on that Day to deniers!” It is the balancing Day where the Balance so people may administer justice is realized, and where submitted are not treated like the wicked, how do you judge, is answered.\n\nThis follows for which Day to name it, and precedes what will make you realize what the Day of Decision is, magnifying.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think Final Decision is arbitrary, like the despicable’s oaths as shields. Final Decision is flawless, as with the Pen and what everyone writes and the well-preserved Record.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid placed in secure place until appointed time, Final Decision is the ultimate appointed time. To have it decide for you as Gardens held in honour where fruit hangs within reach, be among the grateful who fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, give food despite desire, and fear the distressful Day, so Final Decision separates you toward mercy, not toward Hell’s mightiest catastrophe warning to humankind.\n\nFurther: Day of Final Decision also is the Day the deniers see as far but We see as near, the Day the challenger demanded punishment bound to come averted by none from the Lord of pathways, and the Day they will be presented with no secrets hidden. Final Decision, or “fasl,” is the separating, as with angels distinguishing fully and delivering to end excuses, and submitted not wicked, how do you judge. To have Final Decision decide for you as Gardens held in honour where you ask about the wicked, be among the grateful who fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, give food despite desire, and fear the distressful Day, so Final Decision separates you toward mercy, not toward Hell’s mightiest catastrophe.",
  "14": "\"And what will make you realize what the Day of Decision is?\" magnifies the Day after naming it, similar to “What will make you realize what the Inevitable, what Hell is?” The question shows need for revelation.\n\n“And what will make you realize what the Day of Decision is?” translates the same formula used for the Night of Decree, the Inevitable, and Saqar, indicating the reality exceeds imagination without prophetic informing, as with “That knowledge is with Allah alone, and I am only a clear warner” and the Pen.\n\nThis follows Day of Final Decision to emphasize its weight, as with stars put out, sky torn, mountains blown.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to attempt realization via speculation, as with copying the Record in the unseen or demanding punishment bound to come. Realization comes via the described destruction of earlier and later disbelievers, creation from humble fluid, earth as lodging, etc., which the Quran then details.\n\nFor the living, let “what will make you realize” humble you to listen and reason, so you are not among residents of Blaze who lament if only we had listened, but among the mindful who take the Right Way, recite what is easy, and are among the bright faces looking at their Lord when the Day of Decision realizes as Gardens held in honour, not as woe to deniers.\n\nAdditional: What will make you realize what the Day of Decision is also signals that realization requires revelation, not imagination, as with “That knowledge is with Allah alone, and I am only a clear warner” for when the threat will come, and the Pen. Realization is not from the powerless force that would help, the despicable oath-taker, or the ancient fables dismissal. It comes via the described destruction of earlier and later disbelievers, creation from humble fluid, earth as lodging, and the nineteen keepers. Let “what will make you realize” humble you to listen and reason, so you are not among residents of Blaze who lament if only we had listened, but among those in Gardens held in honour where realization is bliss.",
  "15": "\"Woe on that Day to the deniers!\" pronounces woe after magnifying the Day of Decision. The refrain repeats throughout the surah.\n\n“Woe on that Day to the deniers!” translates “waylun yawma’idhin li-l-mukadhdhibin,” woe that Day to those who called true false, who denied what is yet to come, asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and said “Allah has revealed nothing. You are extremely astray,” and “ancient fables” and “pure magic” when the foretold prophet came, and who equated submitted and wicked.\n\nWoe, or “wayl,” is destruction, as with woe and more woe for the denier who neither believed nor prayed, woe to us we have been transgressors after garden ashes, and woe to the despicable withholder. On that Day, day is the Day of Decision, the promised will come to pass.\n\nDeniers, or “mukadhdhibin,” are those who denied, as with the challenger demanding punishment, the deniers who love fleeting and neglect weighty Day, and the spooked zebras fleeing reminder.\n\nThis follows what will make you realize, showing that woe is the realization for deniers.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear woe as curse from people. It is divine pronouncement, as with the formidable severe angels over the Fire.\n\nFor practice, do not be a denier. Be among those who believed the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance, who will never associate, who gave rightful share, and who walk upright, so woe on that Day is not yours, but Gardens held in honour, bliss, and vast kingdom where woe is replaced by radiance and joy, and striving appreciated.\n\nMore: Woe on that Day to the deniers also marks the Day of Decision as the Day of mutual loss and gain, the Day they see as far but We see as near, the Day the sky is molten brass, mountains wool, no close friend asks, and the wicked wish to ransom with everyone. Woe, or “wayl,” is destruction, as with woe and more woe for the denier who neither believed nor prayed, and woe to us after garden ashes. Deniers here are those who denied what is yet to come, asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and said “Allah has revealed nothing. You are extremely astray.” To avoid woe, be among those who believed the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance, who will never associate, and who are properly observant, whose Gardens are held in honour.",
  "16": "\"Did We not destroy earlier disbelievers?\" reminds after woe that the Day of Decision is not abstract, but has historical precedent. The question is rhetorical, expecting “Yes.”\n\n“Did We not destroy earlier disbelievers?” translates the reminder that We destroyed earlier, as with Thamud’s overwhelming blast, ‘Ad’s furious wind seven nights and eight days like uprooted palms, Pharaoh and those before him and the overturned cities crushing grip, societies that rebelled and were called to severe account, tasted total loss, and the garden reduced to ashes while they slept. Earlier disbelievers are the former nations who denied the messengers’ time to testify and thought strongholds put them out of reach.\n\nThis follows woe on that Day to show woe is not new, and precedes “And We will make the later disbelievers follow them,” showing continuity.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat earlier destruction as mythic ancient fables. Earlier destruction is the way of Our punishment in this world, far worse in Hereafter if only they knew, and the severe punishment prepared.\n\nFor the living who are told this is a reminder so let whoever wills take the Right Way, earlier destruction should make you take it, not deny as earlier did. Be among the grateful who fulfil vows, whose Gardens’ shade is right above, not among earlier disbelievers destroyed whose way you would follow to follow them.\n\nExtra: Did We not destroy earlier disbelievers also recalls Thamud’s blast, ‘Ad’s wind seven nights and eight days like uprooted palms, Pharaoh and overturned cities crushing grip, societies tasting total loss, and garden ashes. Earlier disbelievers are the former nations who denied the messengers’ time, thought strongholds out of reach, and indulged until they faced their Day. This woe is not new, but follows the way of Our punishment in this world, far worse in Hereafter if only they knew. For the living who are told this is a reminder so let whoever wills take the Right Way, earlier destruction should make you take it, not deny, so you are among the grateful whose Gardens’ shade is right above, not among earlier disbelievers destroyed whose way you would follow.",
  "17": "\"And We will make the later disbelievers follow them.\" adds that later deniers will share the earlier’s fate after stating earlier destruction. The pattern continues.\n\n“And We will make the later disbelievers follow them” translates that We will make the later follow the earlier in destruction, as with “We will make the later disbelievers follow them” indicates the Meccans, the hypocrites, the luxe deniers, the despicable withholder, and any who persist in denial and turn away, who indulge and amuse until they face their Day, will follow Thamud and ‘Ad, Pharaoh and the overturned. Follow, or “nutbi‘uhum,” is to make succeed, to bring later upon earlier, as with the gentle wind successive and the angels delivering successively, but here in punishment.\n\nThis follows earlier destruction to show that the Day of Decision’s woe is not limited to ancients, but includes the present deniers who rush headlong to mock from right and left, expecting Garden without being among those who pray.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think later following is predestined without choice to take the Right Way. Following is for those who choose to deny, as with “to whichever chooses to take the lead or lag,” and “let whoever wills be mindful, but they cannot unless Allah wills, He is worthy to be feared.”\n\nFor practice, do not follow earlier disbelievers. Follow the messengers, the noble Messenger reciting, the jinn who believed, and the grateful who fed despite desire. That following makes you among the people of the right in Gardens asking about the wicked, not among later disbelievers made to follow the earlier into chains, shackles, and blazing Fire.\n\nFurther: Later disbelievers follow them also warns the Meccans, the hypocrites, the luxury deniers, the despicable withholder, and any who persist in denial and turn away, indulging and amusing until they face their Day, will follow Thamud and ‘Ad into woe. Follow, or “nutbi‘uhum,” is to make later succeed earlier in destruction, as with successive winds and angels delivering successively, but here in punishment. To not follow, follow the messengers, the noble Messenger, the jinn who believed, and the grateful who fed despite desire, so following makes you among the people of the right in Gardens asking about the wicked, not among later disbelievers made to follow earlier into chains and blazing Fire.",
  "18": "\"This is how We deal with the wicked.\" generalizes the pattern of destroying earlier and making later follow, after the Day of Decision’s woe. The dealing is principle.\n\n“This is how We deal with the wicked” translates “kadhalika naf‘alu bi-l-mujrimin,” thus We do with the wicked, the same as with Thamud, ‘Ad, Pharaoh, overturned. Wicked, or “mujrimin,” are those who cut themselves off through sin, who gathered and hoarded, who turned backs and hoarded, whose wealth did not benefit and authority stripped, who were told seize and shackle then burn and chain seventy arms, for never having faith in the Greatest nor encouraging feeding the poor.\n\nThis follows earlier and later to show that wicked’s treatment is consistent, not arbitrary, as with every soul detained for what it has done and the balance so people may administer justice.\n\nHow We deal indicates the well-preserved Record and the Pen, the appointed time that never delays, and the overwhelming punishment for turning from remembrance.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear this as collective punishment without individual will. Wicked are wicked by choosing to deny, as with the denier who neither believed nor prayed but denied and turned away.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid placed in secure place until appointed time, wicked dealing should deter. Choose not wicked but submitted, not fuel for Hell but seeker of right course, so “This is how We deal with the wicked” is not your dealing, but the dealing you are delivered from with radiance and joy, Garden and silk, reclining, shade, fruit, silver, crystal, ginger, Salsabil, eternal youths, bliss and kingdom, where your dealing is “All this is surely a reward for you. Your striving has been appreciated.”\n\nMore: How We deal with the wicked also generalizes that wicked’s treatment is consistent, not arbitrary, as with every soul detained for what it has done and the balance so people may administer justice. Wicked, or “mujrimin,” are those who gathered and hoarded, turned backs, whose wealth did not benefit and authority stripped, told seize and shackle then burn and chain. How We deal is the well-preserved Record and the Pen, the appointed time that never delays, and the overwhelming punishment for turning from remembrance. To avoid this dealing, choose not wicked but submitted, not fuel for Hell but seeker of right course, so dealing is not your woe but the dealing you are delivered from with radiance and Gardens held in honour, where your dealing is “All this is surely a reward, your striving appreciated.”",
  "19": "\"Woe on that Day to the deniers!\" repeats the refrain after stating how We deal with the wicked. The woe returns as emphasis.\n\n“Woe on that Day to the deniers!” again marks the Day of Decision, the promised will come to pass, stars put out, sky torn, mountains blown, messengers timed. Woe is repeated as a chorus, like the garden owners’ double “How evil was what he determined” and the woe to you, and more woe, and again woe.\n\nDeniers are those who denied what is yet to come, who asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and who thought Allah would not resurrect.\n\nThis follows how We deal with the wicked to apply woe to that dealing, and precedes “Did We not create you from a humble fluid?” which shifts to creation as proof.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to tire of repetition. Repetition is for rhythm and warning, as with the Reminder that would humble a mountain and the Pen.\n\nFor the living, let repeated woe move you to repeated mindfulness, morning and evening remembrance, night prostration long, so woe on that Day is not yours, but the Gardens held in honour where woe is replaced by “Eat and drink joyfully for what you did in days gone by,” and where the wicked’s answer “We were not of those who prayed” is not yours because you were among those who prayed consistently and properly observant.\n\nAdditional: Woe on that Day to the deniers again emphasizes the Day of mutual loss and gain, the promised will come to pass, the stars put out, sky torn, mountains blown. Woe repeated is rhythm for warning, as with the Reminder that would humble a mountain and the Pen. To let repeated woe move you to repeated mindfulness, morning and evening remembrance, night prostration long, so woe on that Day is not yours, but the Gardens held in honour where woe is replaced by “Eat and drink joyfully for what you did in days gone by,” and the wicked’s “We were not of those who prayed” is not yours because you prayed consistently and properly observant.",
  "20": "\"Did We not create you from a humble fluid,\" asks after woe, shifting from cosmic signs and historical destruction to personal origin, similar to “But no! Indeed, they already know what We created them from.” The humble fluid humbles the denier who expects Garden without being among those who pray.\n\n“Did We not create you from a humble fluid” translates “alam nakhluqkum min ma’in mahin,” did We not create you from despised water, the same nutfah, sperm-drop, mixed fluids, humble, low, like the garden’s “like a plant” growth. Humble fluid, or “ma’in mahin,” is the fluid the denier knows, as with We created you yet some are disbelievers while some are believers and He is All-Seeing, and He shaped you perfecting form, and He created seven heavens one above another without flaw.\n\nHumble fluid is the opposite of abundant wealth, children always by his side, and made very easy that made him hungry for more and stubborn.\n\nThis follows woe to deniers to remind that the denier’s origin is humble, so expecting Garden of Bliss without being among those who pray is delusion, like honour expels inferior.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear humble fluid as insult. It humbles to make you grateful, as with the self-reproaching soul and the attentive ear.\n\nFor practice, remember humble fluid when you are told to make room, to give rightful share, to walk spacious pathways, so humility makes you among the grateful whose Gardens’ shade is right above, where humble origin becomes vast kingdom and bliss, not chains, shackles, and blazing Fire prepared for the ungrateful.\n\nFurther: Did We not create you from a humble fluid also humbles the denier who expects Garden without being among those who pray, gives rightful share, and walks upright. Humble fluid, or “ma’in mahin,” is the despised fluid the denier knows, as with We created you yet some are disbelievers and He is All-Seeing, and He shaped you perfecting form, and the seven heavens without flaw. Humble fluid is the opposite of abundant wealth, children always by his side, and made very easy that made him hungry for more and stubborn. Remembering humble fluid should make you give rightful share, walk spacious pathways, and take the Right Way, so humble origin becomes vast kingdom and bliss, not chains, shackles, blazing Fire for the ungrateful.",
  "21": "\"placing it in a secure place\" details where the humble fluid is placed, the womb, the secure lodging.\n\n“placing it in a secure place” translates “fa-ja‘alnahu fi qararin makin,” then We placed it in a firm, secure settlement, the womb, as with the secure place until appointed time, the lodging earth for the living and the dead, and the secure place until an appointed time where We perfectly ordained its development. Secure, or “makin,” is firm, protected, like the well-preserved Record touched only by purified angels and the Pen, and the Gardens held in honour.\n\nPlacing it in a secure place shows the Most Capable who holds all authority and creates death and life to test, the King, Holy, who smooths earth and holds birds.\n\nThis follows humble fluid to show that even humble fluid is placed securely, not left without purpose, as with “Do people think they will be left without purpose? Were they not once a sperm-drop emitted?”\n\nSecure place until an appointed time indicates the appointed time that never delays when it comes and can never be delayed, if only you knew, and the Day fifty thousand years.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to limit secure place to biology without moral weight. Secure place is the test’s cradle, where hearing and seeing are made, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful chosen.\n\nFor the one who was nothing worth mentioning, then a drop, secure place is mercy, as with the Ark carried when floodwater overflowed as reminder for attentive ears. Use security to be grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, so secure place leads to secure Gardens, not to chains, and the appointed time finds you among the bright faces looking at their Lord.\n\nExtra: Placing it in a secure place also shows the Most Capable who holds all authority and creates death and life to test, the King, Holy, who smooths earth and holds birds. Secure, or “makin,” is firm, protected, like the well-preserved Record only purified touch, the Gardens held in honour, and the Pen. Secure place until appointed time is the appointed time that never delays, the Day of Decision set, the Day every soul detained except the people of the right. Use security to be grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, so secure place leads to secure Gardens, not to chains, and the appointed time finds you among bright faces looking at their Lord.",
  "22": "\"until an appointed time?\" asks the duration of the secure place after humble fluid. The time is fixed.\n\n“until an appointed time?” translates “ila qadarin ma‘lum,” until a known measure, an appointed term, as with the appointed time delay until which forgiveness was offered to Noah’s people if they worship, fear, obey, the delay until appointed time that can never be delayed when it comes, the appointed time for humble fluid in the secure place, the appointed time for earth as lodging, and the appointed time for the Day of Decision set.\n\nKnown measure, or “ma‘lum,” is known to Allah, the Knower of unseen, All-Knowing, All-Wise who determines day and night and writes every calamity or blessing before creation.\n\nThis follows secure place to show that security has a term, not indefinite, as with the respite for a little while for luxury deniers left to Me.\n\nAppointed time indicates that the Day promised will come to pass is appointed, the Trumpet’s blast is appointed, and is easy for Allah.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think appointed time is negotiable like the despicable’s oaths. It is not, as with “We cannot be prevented from transforming.”\n\nFor the living who love fleeting and neglect the weighty Day, appointed time should make you urgent. The humble fluid’s appointed time in the secure place ends with birth; your appointed time in the world ends with presentation where no secret stays hidden. Use appointed time to be among the grateful who fulfil, fear, feed, and are delivered, rewarded with Garden and silk, where appointed becomes “All this is surely a reward for you.”\n\nMore: Until an appointed time also indicates that the Day set is appointment, the Trumpet’s blast is appointed, and is easy for Allah. Known measure, or “ma‘lum,” is known to the Knower of unseen, All-Knowing, All-Wise who determines day and night and writes every calamity or blessing before creation. Until an appointed time shows security has a term, not indefinite, as with respite for a little while for luxury deniers left to Me. Appointed time should make you urgent, the humble fluid’s appointed time in secure place ends with birth; your appointed time in the world ends with presentation where no secret stays hidden. Use appointed time to be among the grateful who fulfil, fear, feed, and are delivered, rewarded with Garden and silk, where appointed becomes “All this is surely a reward for you.”",
  "23": "\"We ˹perfectly˺ ordained ˹its development˺. How excellent are We in doing so!\" states the perfection of the appointed time’s development. The verse praises the Ordainer.\n\n“We perfectly ordained its development. How excellent are We in doing so!” translates “fa-qadarna fa-ni‘ma al-qadirun,” then We determined, measured, and how excellent are the Determiners, the Capable. Qadarna is to measure precisely, as with the Pen and what everyone writes, the well-preserved Record, the appointed time that never delays, and the silver crystalline filled precisely as desired.\n\nPerfectly ordained indicates that the humble fluid’s secure place until appointed time is measured, shaped, as with He developed and perfected their form, He shaped you perfecting form, and the seven heavens without flaw.\n\nHow excellent are We in doing so praises the Most Capable, the Blessed in Whose Hands rests all authority, the Lord of easts and wests truly capable to replace and cannot be prevented.\n\nThis follows until an appointed time to show that the One who sets time also measures perfectly within it.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear “How excellent are We” as boast. It is divine praise that invites you to glorify the Name of your Lord, the Greatest, and to take Him as Trustee.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid, perfectly ordained should make you grateful, show Way, choose grateful, fulfill vows, give food despite desire, so perfectly ordained becomes your Gardens held in honour where fruit is easy, shade above, silver vessels precisely filled, and ginger from Salsabil, all perfectly ordained as Gardens, not as chains and blazing Fire.\n\nFurther: Perfectly ordained also praises the Most Capable, the Blessed in Whose Hands rests all authority, the Lord of easts and wests truly capable to replace. Perfectly ordained is measured, as with the Pen and what everyone writes, the well-preserved Record, the appointed time that never delays, and the silver crystalline filled precisely as desired. Perfectly ordained is excellent, as with How excellent are We in doing so praising the Ordainer. To see perfectly ordained as excellent, be grateful, show Way, choose grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, so perfectly ordained becomes your Gardens held in honour where fruit is easy, shade above, silver vessels precisely filled, and ginger from Salsabil, all perfectly ordained as Gardens, not chains.",
  "24": "\"Woe on that Day to the deniers!\" again marks the refrain after praising perfect ordainment. The woe returns.\n\n“Woe on that Day to the deniers!” again for the Day of Decision, after creation from humble fluid, secure place, appointed time, perfect ordainment. Deniers are those who denied what is yet to come, asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and equated submitted and wicked.\n\nThis follows How excellent are We to contrast. Perfect ordainment is excellent, but denying it earns woe.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to tire of woe’s repetition. Woe repeated is rhythm that hammers, like the Pen and the mountain.\n\nFor the grateful who see perfectly ordained as how excellent, woe is not yours, but the bliss and vast kingdom, where your ordainment is Garden, not Fire.\n\nExtra: Woe on that Day to the deniers again after perfect ordainment contrasts perfect ordainment’s excellence with denying it earns woe. Perfect ordainment excellent, but denying it earns woe. Woe repeated is hammer, like the Pen and the mountain. For the grateful who see perfectly ordained as how excellent, woe is not yours, but bliss and vast kingdom, where ordainment is Garden, not Fire.\n\nFurther, this woe after perfect ordainment also highlights that perfect measuring includes the secure place until appointed time for humble fluid, and the earth as lodging for living and dead, both perfectly ordained with known measure. Excellent ordaining is the reason to glorify the Greatest, to take Him as Trustee, and to devote wholeheartedly. Denying it earns woe because it denies the Most Capable who holds all authority and who can replace with others better and cannot be prevented. To turn woe into Gardens held in honour, see perfectly ordained as excellent, be grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, and fear the sweeping horror, so the promise will come to pass as Gardens where fruit is made very easy to reach and silver vessels are filled precisely as desired, not as chains, shackles, and blazing Fire.",
  "25": "\"Have We not made the earth a lodging\" asks after woe, shifting from personal creation to earthly dwelling, the secure place writ large.\n\n“Have We not made the earth a lodging” translates “alam naj‘ali al-arda kifata,” did We not make earth a container, a lodging, as with the earth a lodging for the living and the dead, the earth smoothed for you to move about and eat from provision and to Him is resurrection, and the earth spread for spacious pathways to walk. Lodging, or “kifata,” is to gather, to hold, as with the Gardens held in honour, the well-preserved Record, and the Pen.\n\nEarth as lodging echoes the secure place that held humble fluid until appointed time, now holding humanity, living and dead, until appointed time.\n\nHave We not is rhetorical expecting “Yes, indeed.”\n\nThis follows perfect ordainment to show that the One who perfectly ordained humble fluid also lodges you on earth.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to take lodging as mere dirt, not as mercy that holds.\n\nFor the living who love fleeting, earth as lodging should remind you to take the Right Way while you will, before you become among the dead earth lodges, so lodging becomes the elevated Garden’s vast kingdom, not the raging Flame that rips scalps where no lodging is safe.\n\nAdditional: Earth a lodging also mirrors the secure place that held humble fluid until appointed time, now holding humanity, living and dead, until appointed time. Earth as lodging for the living walking spacious pathways and for the dead returned to it and brought forth again, as with growing from earth like a plant. Have We not is rhetorical expecting “Yes, indeed.” Lodging is to gather, to hold, as with Gardens held in honour, Record well-preserved, and Pen. Earth as lodging should remind you to take the Right Way while you will, before you become among the dead earth lodges, so lodging becomes the elevated Garden’s vast kingdom, not the raging Flame that rips scalps where no lodging is safe.",
  "26": "\"for the living and the dead,\" clarifies earth’s lodging after asking Have We not made earth a lodging. The lodging holds both.\n\n“for the living and the dead” translates “ahya’an wa amwata,” living and dead, as with the humble fluid placed in secure place until appointed time, then perfectly ordained, then earth as lodging for living walking spacious pathways and for dead returned to it and brought forth again, as with growing from earth like a plant. Living and dead indicates earth gathers all, like the Day He will gather you all for mutual loss and gain, the Day fifty thousand years, the Trumpet.\n\nThis follows earth lodging to show its comprehensiveness, and precedes mountains as pegs, rivers, etc., but here directly it serves as proof for the deniers who will have woe, that the One who lodges living and dead can reassemble bones and fingertips, is such a Creator unable to bring the dead back?\n\nA misunderstanding would be to see lodging for dead as merely burial. It is also the cradle for resurrection, as with the Ark carried when floodwater overflowed and attentive ears grasp.\n\nFor practice, remember you are among the living earth lodges, so move about its regions and eat provision knowing to Him is resurrection, be among those who give rightful share to the asker and deprived, and walk upright, so lodging for the dead becomes for you the Gardens lodged in honour where the living are in a life of bliss, not the chains, shackles, and blazing Fire that await the ungrateful.\n\nMore: For the living and the dead also shows earth gathers all, like the Day He will gather you all for mutual loss and gain, the Day fifty thousand years, the Trumpet. Living and dead indicates comprehensive, as with humble fluid placed in secure place until appointed time, then perfectly ordained, then earth as lodging. This is proof for the deniers who will have woe, that the One who lodges living and dead can reassemble bones and fingertips, is such a Creator unable? Use living lodging to move about regions and eat provision knowing to Him is resurrection, be among those who give rightful share to the asker and deprived, and walk upright, so lodging for the dead becomes for you the Gardens lodged in honour where living are in a life of bliss.",
  "27": "\"and placed upon it towering, firm mountains, and given you fresh water to drink?\" continues the question after earth as lodging for living and dead. The verse pairs mountains and fresh water.\n\n“and placed upon it towering, firm mountains, and given you fresh water to drink?” translates “wa ja‘alna fiha rawasiya shamikhatin wa asqaynakum ma’an furata,” did We not place firm, lofty mountains and give you sweet water? Towering firm mountains, or “rawasiya shamikhat,” are pegs that stabilize, as with the mountains blown away like tufts of wool on the Day, and dunes of shifting sand when earth shakes. Fresh water, or “ma’an furata,” is sweet, palatable, as with the abundant rain showered after seeking forgiveness, gardens and rivers supplied, spring flowing at will, flowing water if yours sinks who else could bring it, and the Pen’s water.\n\nThis pair follows earth lodging to show that the One who lodges living and dead also pegs earth with mountains and gives drinkable water, not salty that could be made salty, all perfectly ordained.\n\nThe question is rhetorical expecting “Yes, indeed,” as with humble fluid placed in secure place and perfectly ordained, excellent.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to take mountains and fresh water as mere geography. They are signs that the One who can give fresh water to drink can also make water sink then bring flowing water, and who can place mountains can blow them away.\n\nFor the living who love fleeting and neglect weighty Day, mountains and fresh water should inspire awe of Majesty who created you in stages, seven heavens, moon and sun, growth like plant, return and bringing forth, spread pathways, so you fulfil vows, give food despite desire, and fear the sweeping horror, rather than deny. Using fresh water with thanks, giving rightful share, and walking spacious pathways with purpose makes mountains and water your Gardens’ shade and springs amid cool shade, not your woe on that Day to deniers.",
  "28": "\"Woe on that Day to the deniers!\" again after mountains and fresh water. The woe returns as refrain.\n\n“Woe on that Day to the deniers!” again for the Day of Decision, after creation from humble fluid, secure place, appointed time, perfect ordainment, earth lodging, mountains and fresh water. Deniers are those who denied what is yet to come, asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and will be among the wicked asked what landed you in Hell, not praying, not feeding poor.\n\nThis follows mountains and water to show that denying these signs earns woe, as with earlier woe after perfect ordainment.\n\nWoe is the same woe as for the despicable withholder and the garden owners’ “How evil was what he determined,” but on the Day it is declared.\n\nFor the grateful who see mountains and fresh water as signs, woe is not theirs, but the shade and springs amid cool shade for the righteous who will have Gardens, as next describes, where fruit desired is theirs and they are told to eat and drink happily for what they used to do.\n\nFurther, woe after mountains and fresh water also shows that even after the One who lodges living and dead, places firm mountains, and gives sweet water to drink, woe remains for those who deny. Mountains and water are signs that the One who can give fresh water can also make water sink then bring flowing water, and who can place mountains can blow them away. For the grateful who see these as signs, woe is not theirs, but cool shade and springs amid the righteous. To avoid woe, be among those who fulfil vows, fear the sweeping horror, give food despite desire for Allah alone, and fear the distressful Day, so woe is replaced by “Eat and drink happily” and “All this is surely a reward, your striving appreciated.”",
  "29": "\"˹The disbelievers will be told,˺ “Proceed into that ˹Fire˺ which you used to deny!\" voices the command to the deniers on the Day, after woe. The Fire is what they denied.\n\n“The disbelievers will be told, ‘Proceed into that Fire which you used to deny!’” translates the address to those who denied what is yet to come, asked “When is the Day?” mocked as ancient fables, pure magic, and thought Allah would not resurrect. Fire which you used to deny is the same Fire that almost bursts, raging Flame ripping scalps, Hell that does not let live, scorching skin, nineteen keepers, mighty catastrophe warning to humankind, choking food, dunes, and the seven nights and eight days wind. Used to deny indicates habitual denial, as with persisting in denial and acting very arrogantly, pressing fingers, covering.\n\nProceed, or “intaliqu,” is to go, to set forth, as with the Day they will come forth from graves swiftly racing to an idol, with eyes downcast covered with disgrace, and the Trumpet’s difficult Day.\n\nThis follows woe to deniers to show what woe is.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear “Proceed” as invitation to explore. It is command to enter, as with “Seize and shackle them, then burn them in Hell, then tie them with chains seventy arms long.”\n\nFor the living who are told this is a reminder so let whoever wills take the Right Way, proceed into Fire is what you avoid by taking the lead, being among the people of the right, the righteous amid cool shade and springs, any fruit they desire, told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, not the woeful deniers.\n\nMore: Proceed into the Fire which you used to deny also answers the earlier question “What is the matter with you? How do you judge? Should We treat submitted like wicked?” The Fire denied is the same Fire that is mightiest catastrophe warning to humankind, the raging Flame ripping scalps, Saqar not letting live, scorching skin, nineteen keepers, and the choking food. Used to deny indicates habitual denial, as with persisting in denial and acting very arrogantly, pressing fingers, covering clothes, and saying “Allah has revealed nothing. You are extremely astray.” To avoid proceeding, proceed now into the Garden’s shade: make room, give rightful share, walk upright, and take the Right Way while you will, so proceeding is to the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, not to the Fire you denied.",
  "30": "\"Proceed into the shade ˹of smoke˺ which rises in three columns,\" details the Fire’s shade after commanding to proceed into the Fire denied. The shade is not mercy.\n\n“Proceed into the shade of smoke which rises in three columns” translates the disbelievers told to go into the shade of smoke that branches into three. Shade of smoke, or “zill dhi thalathi shu‘ab,” is the opposite of the Garden’s shade right above them and never seeing scorching heat, and the extended shade for the people of the right. Three columns indicates it splits into three, like the scattering winds, but here smoke, consistent with the Fire hurling sparks as huge castles and as dark as black camels, and the shade which provides neither coolness nor shelter.\n\nShade of smoke rises as a reminder that even shade, which was mercy for the virtuous, becomes torment for deniers, as with fresh water that could be made salty, and harvest that could be chaff.\n\nThis follows proceed into Fire denied to show Fire’s interior.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think smoke shade offers relief like the Garden’s shade. It is smoke, not coolness, as next clarifies providing neither coolness nor shelter.\n\nFor the righteous who will be amid cool shade and springs, the smoke shade’s three columns warn to avoid woe on that Day to deniers. Choose the Garden’s shade right above and fruit easy, where shade is not smoke but mercy, and you are told to eat and drink happily, not to proceed into smoke that offers no shelter.\n\nExtra: Smoke shade in three columns also mirrors the three postures of the denier who neither believed nor prayed, denied and turned away, then swaggared to his people, and the three denials—ancient fables, pure magic, word of a man. Three columns indicate the smoke branches like the scattering winds, but here for torment, not mercy. Neither coolness nor shelter shows that smoke shade is the opposite of the Garden’s shade right above which provides coolness and the fruit easy to reach, and the extended shade for the people of the right, and the silver vessels. Smoke shade fails because it is from the Fire you denied. To avoid smoke shade, seek the shade that succeeds, the cool shade and springs for the righteous, any fruit they desire, told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, where smoke is nowhere.",
  "31": "\"providing neither coolness nor shelter from the flames.\" qualifies the smoke shade that rises in three columns. The shade fails at both purposes of shade.\n\n“providing neither coolness nor shelter from the flames” translates “la zalil wa la yughni min al-lahab,” no shade, no avail against flame, as with the Garden’s shade right above which provides coolness and the fruit easy that provides nourishment, and the extended shade for the people of the right, and the silver vessels. Neither coolness, or “la zalil,” means the smoke shade does not cool like the Garden never seeing scorching heat, and nor shelter, or “la yughni,” does not protect from flames, like the formidable severe angels over the Fire who never disobey, the raging Flame ripping scalps, and the Fire that does not let live.\n\nThis follows shade of smoke in three columns to show it is worthless.\n\nSmoke shade that neither cools nor shelters mirrors the powerless force that would help instead of the Most Compassionate, and the honour that expels inferior, both delusions that neither cool nor shelter on the Day the soul reaches collar bones and no healer saves.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to imagine smoke shade as at least better than direct flame. It is not; it is part of flame, like choking food and dunes of shifting sand.\n\nFor the living who love fleeting and neglect the weighty Day, this shade warns that not all shade is refuge. Seek the shade that is refuge, the Garden’s shade right above, the cool shade and springs for the righteous, any fruit they desire, told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, so shade provides coolness and shelter because it is from the Most Compassionate in whom we believe and trust, not from the Fire you denied.\n\nMore: Neither coolness nor shelter also answers “which powerless force will help instead of the Most Compassionate? They are lost in delusion” and “who will provide if He withholds? They persist in arrogance.” Coolness and shelter are the two needs that smooth earth lodging, mountains, and fresh water provided, but here both fail. Neither coolness nor shelter shows that the Fire’s shade is not refuge, like the clan that sheltered offered as ransom and everyone on earth together cannot save, and the mountain refuge that does not exist when there will be no refuge and all will end up before your Lord. To find coolness and shelter, be among the righteous amid cool shade and springs, any fruit they desire, whose Gardens are held in honour and whose striving is appreciated, where neither heat nor cold harms.",
  "32": "\"Indeed, it hurls sparks ˹as big˺ as huge castles,\" describes the Fire’s emission after the smoke shade’s failure. The sparks are immense.\n\n“Indeed, it hurls sparks as big as huge castles” translates “innaha tarmu bi-shararin ka-al-qasr,” it throws sparks like a fortress, a palace, huge logs, castles. Hurls, or “tarmu,” is to throw, like shooting stars as missiles against eavesdropping devils and the Pen. Sparks as huge castles indicates size like fortified towers, showing the Fire’s power to throw, as with the furious wind that destroyed ‘Ad and the blast for Thamud, and the Fire that almost bursts, roars as it boils over.\n\nHuge castles contrasts with the Garden’s vast kingdom and bliss, fine green silk, silver bracelets, and pure drink, the true vast kingdom.\n\nThis follows neither coolness nor shelter to show what the smoke shade accompanies, a hurling of fire.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to picture sparks as small embers. Huge castles indicates magnitude that even strongholds thought out of reach cannot withstand.\n\nFor the deniers who left no thought for Allah’s Will and proceeded early fixated, sparks as huge castles are the answer to their fixated purpose. For the virtuous who fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, and give food despite desire, huge castles are not their projectiles, but their Gardens where they recline on canopied couches, never seeing scorching heat, where sparks are replaced by the spring Salsabil and eternal youths as scattered pearls, and the hurling is replaced by being waited on with silver vessels.\n\nFurther: Hurling sparks as huge castles also parallels the shooting stars as missiles against eavesdropping devils that fill heaven with stern guards, and the Pen. Sparks as huge castles show the Fire’s ability to throw, as with the furious wind that destroyed ‘Ad and the blast for Thamud. Huge castles contrasts with the Garden’s vast kingdom and bliss, fine silk, silver bracelets, and pure drink, the true vast kingdom. For the deniers who left no thought for Allah’s Will and proceeded early fixated, sparks as huge castles are the answer to their fixated purpose. For the virtuous who fulfil vows, sparks are replaced by the spring Salsabil and eternal youths as scattered pearls, and the hurling is replaced by being waited on with silver vessels.",
  "33": "\"and ˹as dark˺ as black camels.\" completes the spark description after hurling as huge castles. The colour is dark.\n\n“and as dark as black camels” translates “ka-annahu jimalatun sufr,” like black camels, or yellow camels, dark. Jimalatun sufr are dark, black camels, or a train of camels, showing sparks as dark, smoky, not bright, like the smoke that rises in three columns, providing neither coolness nor shelter. Dark as black camels indicates the sparks are not illuminating like the moon’s reflected light or sun’s radiant lamp within seven heavens, but darkening, as with the moon dimmed and sun and moon brought together, faces gloomy, eyes downcast, and the raging Flame’s dark smoke.\n\nBlack camels as a herd also evokes mass, as with the Day every soul detained, the Day fifty thousand years, and the indulging and amusing until they face their Day.\n\nThis follows huge castles to show that sparks are both huge and dark, not the Garden’s crystal silver, but fire.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to debate camel colour, yellow vs black. The Quran uses the herd’s dark silhouette against fire’s glow to show that sparks are not the Garden’s pearls, but dark masses.\n\nFor the living who were told to make room, give rightful share, and walk upright, dark sparks warn that the Fire’s hurling is dark, while the Garden’s hurling is light, the pure drink from the Lord, the bliss and vast kingdom. Choose the Garden’s light, where woe on that Day to deniers is not yours, but the righteous’ shade and springs are, and you are told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, while dark sparks remain for those who proceeded into the Fire they denied.\n\nMore: Dark as black camels also indicates the sparks’ colour is dark, smoky, not bright like the moon’s reflected light or sun’s radiant lamp within seven heavens, but darkening, as with the moon dimmed and sun and moon brought together, faces gloomy, eyes downcast. Dark as black camels as a herd shows mass, as with the Day every soul detained, the Day fifty thousand years, and indulging until they face their Day. For the living who were told to make room, give rightful share, and walk upright, dark sparks warn that the Fire’s hurling is dark, while the Garden’s hurling is light, the pure drink from the Lord, the bliss and vast kingdom. Choose the Garden’s light, where woe on that Day to deniers is not yours, but the righteous’ shade and springs are.",
  "34": "\"Woe on that Day to the deniers!\" again after describing sparks as huge castles and dark as black camels. The refrain returns.\n\n“Woe on that Day to the deniers!” again for the Day of Decision, after showing smoke shade three columns, neither coolness nor shelter, sparks as castles, dark as camels. Woe is for those who denied what is yet to come, asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and will be among the spooked zebras fleeing reminder, wishing for personal letters, and not fearing Hereafter.\n\nThis follows sparks to apply woe to that Fire.\n\nFor the righteous who will be amid cool shade and springs, woe is not theirs, but the deniers’.\n\nExtra: Woe on that Day to the deniers after sparks as huge castles and dark as black camels marks the Day of Decision, after showing smoke shade three columns, neither coolness nor shelter, sparks as castles and camels. Woe for those who denied what is yet to come, asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and will be spooked zebras fleeing reminder, wishing for personal letters. To avoid woe, be among those who believed the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance, who will never associate, and who are properly observant, whose Gardens are held in honour, where woe is replaced by radiance and joy and striving appreciated.\n\nMore: Woe on that Day to the deniers after sparks as huge castles and dark as black camels marks the Day of Decision, after showing smoke shade three columns, neither coolness nor shelter, sparks as castles and camels. Woe for those who denied what is yet to come, asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and will be spooked zebras fleeing reminder. The Fire’s sparks as huge castles and dark camels are the reality that woe points to, not the Garden’s crystal silver. To avoid woe, be among those who believed the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance, who will never associate, and who are properly observant, whose Gardens are held in honour, where woe is replaced by radiance and joy and striving appreciated, and where smoke shade is replaced by cool shade right above.",
  "35": "\"On that Day they will not ˹be in a position to˺ speak,\" states the silence imposed after sparks and woe. The deniers lose speech.\n\n“On that Day they will not be in a position to speak” translates “hadha yawmu la yantiqun,” this is a Day they will not speak, as with “This is the Day of Final Decision: We have gathered you along with earlier disbelievers for punishment. So if you have a scheme to save yourselves, then use it against Me,” and the presentation where no secret stays hidden and people testify against own souls despite excuses. Not speaking contrasts with “We feed you only for Allah, seeking neither reward nor thanks” spoken by the virtuous, and the Gardens’ asking one another about the wicked.\n\nNot speaking indicates they have no truthful speech left, as with worthless planks that impress but lean, despicable oath-taker, slanderer, and the denier who neither believed nor prayed but denied and swaggered.\n\nThis follows woe to deniers to show that woe includes speechlessness, and precedes nor will they be permitted to offer excuses, showing two denials, not speaking and not excused.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think they are literally mute forever, contradicting “What has landed you in Hell? We were not of those who prayed.” There are stations on the Day, sometimes speaking, sometimes silent.\n\nFor the living, speak now when you can. Remember the Name morning and evening, prostrate part of night, glorify long, give rightful share, and be true to trusts, so on the Day they will not speak, your speaking is the happy “Read my record” in a life of bliss, not silence.\n\nFurther: Not speaking on that Day also contrasts with “We feed you only for Allah, seeking neither reward nor thanks” spoken by the virtuous, and the Gardens’ asking one another about the wicked. Not speaking is imposed silence because they have no truthful speech, as with worthless planks that impress but lean, despicable oath-taker, slanderer, and the denier who neither believed nor prayed but denied and swaggered. Not speaking follows woe to show woe includes speechlessness, and precedes not permitted to offer excuses, showing two denials. To speak on that Day as the happy “Read my record” in a life of bliss, speak now when you can, remember the Name morning and evening, prostrate part of night, glorify long, give rightful share, and be true to trusts.",
  "36": "\"nor will they be permitted to offer excuses.\" adds the second silence after not speaking. Excuses are barred.\n\n“nor will they be permitted to offer excuses” translates “wa la yu’dhanu lahum fa-ya‘tadhirun,” nor will they be given permission to excuse, as with “Make no excuses this Day, you are only rewarded for what you used to do” told to disbelievers after being told to enter the Fire, and “despite the excuses they come up with, the soul is a witness against itself.” Excuses, or “ya‘tadhirun,” are pretexts like “we followed elite whose wealth increases only in loss,” “Do not abandon your idols,” and “we were among the wicked because we indulged.”\n\nThis follows not speaking to show that even if they could speak, excuses would not be permitted, because the time for excuses is before the appointed time that can never be delayed, before the soul reaches collar bones and no healer saves, before woe.\n\nNot permitted indicates that permission to excuse is denied, as with “So the pleas of intercessors will be of no benefit to them” and the intercession that does not benefit the four-cause wicked until the inevitable came.\n\nFor the living who are told this is a reminder so let whoever wills take the Right Way, excuses now can be replaced by sincere repentance that absolves and admits into Gardens, light shines, and striving appreciated, so excuses on that Day are not needed because your record is the joyful “eat and drink for what you did in days gone by.”\n\nMore: Nor permitted to offer excuses also echoes “Make no excuses this Day, you are only rewarded for what you used to do” told to disbelievers, and “despite the excuses they come up with, the soul is a witness against itself.” Excuses are pretexts like “we followed elite whose wealth increases only in loss,” “Do not abandon your idols,” and “we were among the wicked because we indulged.” Not permitted shows the time for excuses is before the appointed time that never delays, before the soul reaches collar bones and no healer saves, before woe. To avoid not being permitted, offer excuses now as sincere repentance that perfects light, where the All-Forgiving, Most Merciful accepts, and the Day they will not speak becomes your Day they will say “Eat and drink happily for what you used to do.”",
  "37": "\"Woe on that Day to the deniers!\" again after not speaking and not permitted to offer excuses. The refrain marks the silence.\n\n“Woe on that Day to the deniers!” again for the Day of Final Decision, after describing the deniers’ speechlessness. Deniers are those whose excuses are barred, who will not speak, whose sparks are huge castles and dark camels, whose shade is smoke three columns neither cool nor shelter.\n\nThis follows silence to emphasise that silence does not save from woe.\n\nFor the righteous who will be amid shade and springs, woe is not theirs.\n\nExtra: Woe on that Day to the deniers after silence and no excuses again marks the Day of Final Decision, where they are silent. Deniers are those whose excuses are barred, who will not speak, whose sparks are huge castles. Woe is destruction, as with woe and more woe for the denier who neither believed nor prayed, and woe to us after garden ashes. For the righteous who will be amid shade and springs, woe is not theirs, but Gardens. To avoid woe, be among the grateful whose striving is appreciated, not among the silent deniers.\n\nAdditional: Woe on that Day to the deniers after silence and no excuses again marks the Day of Final Decision, where they are silent. Deniers are those whose excuses are barred, who will not speak, whose sparks are huge castles. Woe is destruction, as with woe and more woe for the denier who neither believed nor prayed, and woe to us after garden ashes. For the righteous who will be amid shade and springs, woe is not theirs, but Gardens. To avoid woe, be among the grateful whose striving is appreciated, not among the silent deniers. The Day they cannot speak or offer excuses is the same Day they were called to prostrate when fully capable but chose not to, so woe is the recompense for refusing to speak truth when they could.",
  "38": "\"˹They will be told by Allah,˺ “This is the Day of ˹Final˺ Decision: We have gathered you along with earlier disbelievers ˹for punishment˺.\" announces the Day’s identity and gathering, after woe for silent deniers.\n\n“They will be told by Allah, ‘This is the Day of Final Decision: We have gathered you along with earlier disbelievers for punishment’” translates the divine address that identifies the Day set, for which stars put out, sky torn, mountains blown, messengers timed, Day rescheduled. Final Decision, or “yawm al-fasl,” is the separation, distinguishing truth, as with the angels distinguishing fully. Gathered you along with earlier disbelievers parallels “Did We not destroy earlier disbelievers? And We will make later follow them. This is how We deal with the wicked,” showing that gathering includes earlier and later, as with the Day He will gather you all for mutual loss and gain and the Day fifty thousand years.\n\nWe have gathered you indicates the Lord who smooths earth for lodging, places firm mountains, gives fresh water, creates from humble fluid in secure place, perfectly ordains, now gathers.\n\nThis follows woe to deniers to give the gathering that woe points to.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear gathering as merely crowds, not as justice, like rushing headlong in groups to mock. Gathering here is for Final Decision, not for mocking.\n\nFor the living who are told to arise and warn, gathering should motivate taking the Right Way now, so gathering is with the righteous in Gardens asking about the wicked, not with earlier disbelievers for punishment.\n\nAdditional: Day of Final Decision: We have gathered you along with earlier disbelievers also fulfils “Did We not destroy earlier disbelievers? And We will make later follow them. This is how We deal with the wicked.” Gathering along with earlier shows the Day of Gathering for mutual loss and gain, the Day fifty thousand years, the Trumpet, the earth and mountains crushed, sky torn, Throne borne, and presentation with no secrets hidden. We have gathered indicates the Lord who smooths earth for lodging, places firm mountains, gives fresh water, creates from humble fluid in secure place, perfectly ordains, now gathers. To be gathered with the righteous in Gardens asking about the wicked, not with earlier disbelievers for punishment, take the Right Way now, recite what is easy, and be among the mindful who take the lead, not lag.",
  "39": "\"So if you have a scheme ˹to save yourselves˺, then use it against Me.”\" challenges the gathered deniers after announcing the Day of Final Decision and gathering.\n\n“So if you have a scheme to save yourselves, then use it against Me” translates “fa-in kana lakum kaydun fa-kidun,” if you have a plot, then plot against Me. Kayd is scheme, plot, like the tremendous plot devised by the elite who urged idols, who led many astray, and the despicable’s slander and gossip, and the garden owners’ fixated purpose. Scheme to save yourselves is the powerless force that would help instead of the Most Compassionate, the honour that expels inferior, the oaths binding until the Day whatever you decide, and the personal letters wished for.\n\nUse it against Me is a challenge, as with “Bring your associate-gods if truthful,” “Ask them which can guarantee,” and “Do you have a scripture in which you read you will have whatever you choose?” No scheme can succeed against the King, Holy, who holds all authority, Most Capable, whose Hands rest all authority, whose Pen writes, whose angels are stern.\n\nThis follows gathering to show that gathering is the arena where schemes are tested.\n\nIf you have a scheme then use it is like the keepers’ “Did a warner not come?” No scheme will avail, as with no ransom with everyone on earth, no close friend asks, and no intercession benefits.\n\nFor the living, do not rely on schemes like withholding good, feeling secure that One in heaven will not swallow, and calling revelations ancient fables. Instead, take the Right Way, recite what is easy, establish prayer, pay alms, lend good loan, and seek forgiveness, so scheme against Me is not your plan, but sincere repentance that perfects light is.\n\nMore: If you have a scheme to save yourselves, then use it against Me is the challenge to the gathered deniers who devised tremendous plot urging idols, who led many astray, and whose wealth increased only in loss. Scheme, or “kayd,” is like the despicable’s slander and gossip, the garden owners’ fixated purpose, and the hypocrites’ oaths as shields. Use it against Me is as with “Bring your associate-gods if truthful,” “Ask them which can guarantee,” and “Do you have a scripture in which you read whatever you choose?” No scheme can succeed against the King, Holy, who holds all authority, Most Capable, whose Pen writes, whose angels are stern. To have a scheme that succeeds, have the scheme that is sincere repentance that perfects light, not the plot that leads to Saqar.",
  "40": "\"Woe on that Day to the deniers!\" again after the scheme challenge. The refrain marks the gathering and challenge.\n\n“Woe on that Day to the deniers!” again for the Day of Final Decision, where they are gathered with earlier disbelievers and challenged to use a scheme.\n\nDeniers here are the schemers who devised tremendous plot, whose wealth increased only in loss, who urged idols and led many astray.\n\nWoe is the same woe as for those who indulged and amused until they faced their Day, eyes downcast, racing to an idol.\n\nFor the righteous, woe is not theirs.\n\nExtra: Woe on that Day to the deniers after the scheme challenge marks that no scheme saved. Deniers are the schemers who devised tremendous plot, whose wealth increased only in loss, who urged idols and led many astray. Woe is the same woe as for those who indulged until they faced their Day, eyes downcast, racing to an idol. For the righteous, woe is not theirs, but cool shade and springs. To avoid woe, abandon schemes like withholding good and calling ancient fables, and take the Right Way, recite what is easy, establish prayer, pay alms, lend good loan, and seek forgiveness, so scheme against Me is not your plan, but sincere repentance that perfects light is, and woe becomes Gardens held in honour.\n\nFurther: Woe on that Day to the deniers after the scheme challenge marks that no scheme saved. Deniers are the schemers who devised tremendous plot, whose wealth increased only in loss, who urged idols and led many astray. Woe is the same woe as for those who indulged until they faced their Day, eyes downcast, racing to an idol. For the righteous, woe is not theirs, but cool shade and springs. To avoid woe, abandon schemes like withholding good and calling ancient fables, and take the Right Way, recite what is easy, establish prayer, pay alms, lend good loan, and seek forgiveness, so scheme against Me is not your plan, but sincere repentance that perfects light is, and woe becomes Gardens held in honour where the scheme is not needed.",
  "41": "\"Indeed, the righteous will be amid ˹cool˺ shade and springs\" begins the righteous’ counter-scene after woe and scheme. The righteous are now shown, as with the virtuous with camphor drink.\n\n“Indeed, the righteous will be amid cool shade and springs” translates “inna al-muttaqina fi zilalin wa ‘uyun,” the God-conscious among shades and springs, as with the Garden’s shade right above and fruit easy, the canopied couches never seeing scorching heat or bitter cold, the shade and springs for the virtuous, and the Gardens of Bliss with their Lord, the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, and the Gardens under rivers for ever and ever.\n\nCool shade, or “zilal,” is the opposite of the smoke shade three columns that provides neither coolness nor shelter, and the raging Flame ripping scalps. Springs, or “‘uyun,” are sources like Salsabil and the spring flowing at will where servants drink, the abundant rain, and the rivers given with gardens after seeking forgiveness.\n\nRighteous, or “muttaqin,” are those who fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, give food despite desire, fear the distressful Day, pray consistently, give rightful share, believe firmly, guard chastity, keep trusts, and are properly observant, whose Gardens are held in honour.\n\nThis follows woe to deniers to show the contrast, as with residents of Fire not equal residents of Paradise.\n\nFor the one created from humble fluid placed in secure place until appointed time, perfectly ordained, earth as lodging, mountains and fresh water, the righteous’ shade and springs are the reward for being among the grateful who chose grateful, so shade is yours if you are among the mindful who take the Right Way, recite what is easy, and seek forgiveness, where striving is appreciated and pure drink waits.\n\nMore: Cool shade and springs also completes the earlier Garden’s shade right above and fruit easy, the canopied couches never seeing scorching heat, and the Gardens under rivers for ever and ever. Cool shade is the opposite of the smoke shade three columns neither cool nor shelter, and the raging Flame ripping scalps. Springs are Salsabil and the spring flowing at will where servants drink, the abundant rain, and the rivers given with gardens after seeking forgiveness. Cool shade and springs for the righteous, or “muttaqin,” are those who fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, give food despite desire, fear distressful Day, pray consistently, give rightful share, believe firmly, guard chastity, keep trusts, and are properly observant, whose Gardens are held in honour. To be there, be grateful few who choose grateful, so shade and springs become your vast kingdom and bliss.",
  "42": "\"and any fruit they desire.\" adds pleasure to the righteous’ shade and springs. The fruit is unrestricted.\n\n“and any fruit they desire” translates the same as the near fruit that hangs within reach, abundant fruit never out of season, clusters, and the Gardens under rivers for ever and ever where excellent provision is granted. Any fruit they desire indicates variety, as with camphor and ginger drinks, silver vessels precisely filled, and the better garden hoped for after turning.\n\nAny shows that the Garden is not the choking food, painful punishment, and dunes of shifting sand for those left, but the near fruit made very easy.\n\nThis follows cool shade and springs to show that shade and springs come with fruit, the complete Garden.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think any fruit desire is indulgence that would be choking. Any fruit they desire in the Garden is the pure, excellent provision, not the fleeting world’s merchandise better than what is with Allah.\n\nFor the righteous who fulfilled vows, feared sweeping horror, and gave food despite desire, any fruit they desire is the recompense for giving food despite desire in days gone by, so giving in this world becomes fruit desired in the next, and the Day of Decision decides for you as Gardens, not as woe.\n\nExtra: Any fruit they desire also shows variety, as with camphor and ginger drinks, silver vessels precisely filled, and the better garden hoped for after turning. Any fruit they desire is the opposite of the choking food, painful punishment in store, dunes of shifting sand for those left, and the garden reduced to ashes while they slept. Any shows the Garden is not the choking food, dunes, but the near fruit made very easy. For the righteous who fulfilled vows, feared sweeping horror, and gave food despite desire, any fruit they desire is recompense for giving food despite desire in days gone by, so giving in this world becomes fruit desired in the next, and the Day of Decision decides for you as Gardens, not as woe.",
  "43": "\"˹They will be told,˺ “Eat and drink happily for what you used to do.”\" voices the welcome to the righteous amid shade, springs, and any fruit. The command is joyful.\n\n“They will be told, ‘Eat and drink happily for what you used to do’” translates the same as the Gardens’ “Eat and drink joyfully for what you did in days gone by,” and the elevated Garden’s near fruit, and the pure drink from the Lord. Happily, or “hani’an,” is wholesome enjoyment, opposite to choking food and oozing pus that only evildoers eat. For what you used to do indicates recompense, the striving appreciated, the good sent forth found with Allah better and greater, the vows fulfilled, fear of sweeping horror, food given despite desire for Allah alone, perseverance with Garden and silk, radiance and joy.\n\nThis follows any fruit they desire to show that fruit is told to be eaten happily.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear “for what you used to do” as wage that obliges the Most Compassionate. It is reward, favour He grants to whoever He wills, Lord of infinite bounty, but earned through grateful choice.\n\nFor the living who were nothing, then a drop, shown the Way, this tells you what to do to be told this. Fulfil vows, fear the Day, give food despite desire for Allah alone, be among those in Gardens held in honour, so “Eat and drink happily” is your hearing on the Day the righteous are amid cool shade, not the deniers’ woe, and the difficult Day far from easy becomes easy for you.\n\nFurther: Eat and drink happily for what you used to do also mirrors the elevated Garden’s near fruit, the pure drink from the Lord, and the excellent provision for ever and ever. Happily, or “hani’an,” is wholesome enjoyment, opposite to choking food and oozing pus that only evildoers eat. For what you used to do indicates recompense, the striving appreciated, the good sent forth found with Allah better and greater, the vows fulfilled, fear of sweeping horror, food given despite desire for Allah alone. To be told this, do it now, fulfil vows, give food despite desire for Allah alone, be among those in Gardens held in honour, so “Eat and drink happily” is your hearing on the Day the righteous are amid cool shade, not the deniers’ woe, and the difficult Day far from easy becomes easy for you.",
  "44": "\"Surely this is how We reward the good-doers.\" generalizes the righteous’ reward after telling them to eat and drink happily. The principle is stated.\n\n“Surely this is how We reward the good-doers” translates “inna kadhalika najzi al-muhsinin,” thus We recompense the doers of good, as with the Garden owners’ hope for a better garden after turning with hope, and as with the virtuous whose striving is appreciated. Good-doers, or “muhsinin,” are those who do ihsan, excellence, as with praying consistently, giving rightful share, being true to trusts, and walking upright, and as with the helpers who loved emigrants and preferred them.\n\nHow We reward indicates the Pen’s precise measure, the well-preserved Record, the appointed time, and the Gardens held in honour, shade and springs, any fruit, eat and drink happily.\n\nThis follows eat and drink happily to show that happily is how We reward.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think good-doing is automatic, like honour that expels inferior. Good-doing is the grateful Way, fulfilling vows, feeding despite desire, fearing distressful Day, delivering from horror with radiance and joy.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown grateful or ungrateful, being among good-doers is the grateful choice, so reward is the cool shade and springs, not the chains, shackles, blazing Fire for the ungrateful, and the Day of Decision decides for you as good, not as woe.\n\nMore: How We reward the good-doers also generalizes that good-doing is the grateful Way, fulfilling vows, feeding despite desire, fearing distressful Day, delivering from horror with radiance and joy. Good-doers, or “muhsinin,” are those who do ihsan, excellence, as with praying consistently, giving rightful share, being true to trusts, and walking upright, and as with the helpers who loved emigrants and preferred them. How We reward is the Pen’s precise measure, the well-preserved Record, the appointed time, and the Gardens held in honour, shade and springs, any fruit, eat and drink happily. To be rewarded, be among good-doers, not deniers, so reward is the cool shade and springs, not the chains, shackles, blazing Fire for the ungrateful, and the Day of Decision decides for you as good, not as woe.",
  "45": "\"˹But˺ woe on that Day to the deniers!\" returns to woe after rewarding good-doers, after shade, springs, fruit, eat and drink happily, and how We reward. The contrast is sharp.\n\n“But woe on that Day to the deniers!” again for the Day of Final Decision, where good-doers are rewarded with cool shade and woe is for deniers who denied what is yet to come, asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and will be spooked zebras.\n\nBut indicates turn, after showing righteous, the deniers’ woe remains.\n\nWoe is the same woe as for the arrogant who turned his back, frowned, scowled, and said magic and word of a man, and for the wicked asked what landed you in Hell, not praying, not feeding, indulging, denying.\n\nFor the living, woe ***** but the previous shows how to avoid it, be among good-doers, not deniers, so woe is not yours.\n\nAdditional: Woe on that Day to the deniers after rewarding good-doers again marks the contrast. Woe is for the deniers who denied what is yet to come, asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and will be spooked zebras. But after showing righteous amid cool shade, the deniers’ woe remains. For the living, woe but the previous shows how to avoid it, be among good-doers, not deniers, so woe is not yours, but the righteous’ shade and springs are. Choose the grateful path, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, fear the sweeping horror, so woe on that Day is not yours, but Gardens held in honour, fruit easy, silver vessels, and pure drink await.\n\nMore: Woe on that Day to the deniers after rewarding good-doers again marks the contrast after shade, springs, fruit, eat and drink happily, and how We reward. Woe is for the deniers who denied what is yet to come, asked mockingly “When is the Day?” and will be spooked zebras. The righteous’ shade and springs contrast with the smoke shade three columns neither cool nor shelter, and the raging Flame ripping scalps. To avoid woe, be among good-doers, not deniers, so woe is not yours, but the righteous’ shade and springs are. Choose the grateful path, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, fear the sweeping horror, so woe on that Day is not yours, but Gardens held in honour, fruit easy, silver vessels, and pure drink await, where woe is replaced by bliss and vast kingdom.",
  "46": "\"“Eat and enjoy yourselves for a little while, ˹for˺ you are truly wicked.”\" addresses the deniers in this world, after woe, contrasting the righteous’ eat and drink happily. The permission is temporary.\n\n“‘Eat and enjoy yourselves for a little while, for you are truly wicked’” translates the same as “let them indulge and amuse until they face their Day” and “leave to Me the deniers, people of luxury, bear with them a little while.” Little while indicates the respite that is short compared to the Day fifty thousand years, the Day the soul reaches collar bones, and the appointed time that never delays. Truly wicked, or “mujrimun,” are those who cut themselves off, gathered and hoarded, turned backs, hoarded, whose dealt dealing is as earlier, whose expectation of Garden without traits is delusion, whose scheme cannot save.\n\nEat and enjoy for a little while for the wicked contrasts with eat and drink happily for what you used to do for the righteous; one is for a little while with guilt, the other for ever and ever with appreciation.\n\nThis follows woe to deniers to show that little while is all they have.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear little while as approval to indulge, as with loving fleeting and neglecting weighty. Little while is warning, as with shackles, raging Fire, choking food in store, and dunes.\n\nFor practice, do not eat and enjoy as the wicked for a little while, withholding good, worshipping wealth, and saying ancient fables. Eat and enjoy as the virtuous who give food despite desire for Allah alone, seeking neither reward nor thanks, fearing the horribly distressful Day, so little while becomes Gardens held in honour where eating is happy for what you did in days gone by, and you are rewarded as good-doers, not told woe.",
  "47": "\"Woe on that Day to the deniers!\" again after the righteous’ reward and the command to eat and enjoy for a little while as wicked. The woe refrains.\n\n“Woe on that Day to the deniers!” again for the Day of Decision, after shade, springs, fruit, eat and drink happily, how We reward good-doers, and eat and enjoy for a little while as wicked. Deniers are those who denied the sweeping horror, who will be told to proceed into the Fire denied, who indulge and amuse until they face their Day, and who are spooked zebras.\n\nWoe here is the same woe as for the arrogant who turned his back, frowned, and said magic.\n\nThis woe follows eat and enjoy for a little while to show little while ends in woe, while eat and drink happily ends in reward.\n\nFor the righteous who will be amid cool shade and springs, woe is not theirs, but for the deniers who love fleeting and neglect weighty Day, woe is theirs. To avoid woe, be among good-doers, not deniers, so woe on that Day is not yours, but Gardens held in honour where woe is replaced by bliss.\n\nFurther, woe after the righteous’ reward and eat and enjoy for a little while as wicked shows that woe is the mirror of eat and drink happily. Woe is for the deniers who denied sweeping horror and horribly distressful Day, whose wealth and children only increase loss, who devised tremendous plot urging idols, and who indulged and amused until they faced their Day. Woe repeated is rhythm for warning, as with the Pen and the mountain, and with the Reminder that would humble a mountain. To avoid woe, be among the grateful who fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, give food despite desire, and fear the distressful Day, so woe is replaced by radiance and Gardens held in honour where woe is not yours.",
  "48": "\"When it is said to them, “Bow down ˹before Allah,” they do not bow.\" describes the deniers’ refusal that earns repeated woe. The bow is the test.\n\n“When it is said to them, ‘Bow down before Allah,’ they do not bow” translates the deniers’ response to the call to prostrate when fully capable but chose not to, eyes downcast covered with disgrace, faces gloomy, the Shin bared and asked to prostrate but cannot, and the call to prostrate when fully capable. Bow down, or “irka‘u,” is to bow, to prostrate, as with the servant of Allah stood up calling upon Him alone, the wrapped standing half the night, and the excepted who pray consistently and properly observant, whose Gardens are held in honour.\n\nThis follows woe to deniers to show why woe is: they were called to bow, the same call as “Remember the Name morning and evening, prostrate part of night, glorify long,” and they did not.\n\nNot bowing is the same as pressing fingers, covering clothes, turning heads in disgust, and persisting in denial.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to limit bowing to physical act. Bowing is submission, as with worship Allah alone, fear Him, obey me, and taking the Right Way.\n\nFor the living who are told this is a reminder so let whoever wills take the Right Way, bowing now is the choice to take the lead. Bow now when you can, prostrate part of night, remember morning and evening, be true to trusts, so on the Day they will not be in a position to speak, you are among those who will be told to eat and drink happily, rewarded as good-doers, not the woeful deniers.\n\nMore: Bow down before Allah also recalls the servant of Allah stood up calling upon Him alone and the pagans almost swarmed, the wrapped standing half the night, and the excepted who pray consistently and properly observant. Bow down is not mere bending, but submission, as with worship Allah alone, fear Him, obey me, and taking the Right Way. When told to bow and they do not bow, the refusal is active, like pressing fingers, covering, persisting, acting arrogantly, re-contemplating, frowning, turning his back, saying magic and word of a man. To bow now is to remember the Name morning and evening, prostrate part of night, glorify long, so bowing on that Day when the Shin is bared is possible, eyes not downcast covered with disgrace, but bright looking at Lord.",
  "49": "\"Woe on that Day to the deniers!\" again after they do not bow when told. The woe follows the refusal.\n\n“Woe on that Day to the deniers!” again for the Day of Decision, after describing the deniers who when told to bow do not bow, similar to the despicable oath-taker, slanderer, and the garden owners fixated. Woe is for those whose excuse is not permitted and who will not speak.\n\nThis follows bowing refusal to apply woe.\n\nFor the righteous amid cool shade, woe is not theirs.\n\nFurther: Woe on that Day to the deniers after not bowing again marks the Day of Decision, after describing the deniers who when told to bow do not bow, similar to the despicable oath-taker, slanderer, and garden owners fixated. Woe is destruction, as with woe and more woe for the denier who neither believed nor prayed, and woe to us after garden ashes. To let repeated woe move you to repeated mindfulness, morning and evening remembrance, night prostration long, so woe on that Day is not yours, but the Gardens held in honour where woe is replaced by “Eat and drink happily for what you used to do” and the wicked’s “We were not of those who prayed” is not yours because you prayed consistently and properly observant, and where the righteous are amid cool shade and springs.\n\nMore: Woe on that Day to the deniers after not bowing again emphasizes that bowing refusal is active, like pressing fingers, covering clothes, persisting, acting arrogantly, re-contemplating, frowning, turning his back, saying magic. Woe on that Day is the recompense for not bowing when called before the Lord of east and west, the King, Holy, whose Hands hold authority, Most Capable, who smoothed earth, pegged mountains, created pairs, gave sleep, night, day, seven heavens, shining lamp, pouring water, grain, orchards, and appointed Day of Decision. To avoid woe, bow now when you can, prostrate part of night, remember morning and evening, be true to trusts, so woe on that Day is not yours, but Gardens where you are told to eat and drink happily for what you did in days gone by.",
  "50": "\"So what message after this ˹Quran˺ would they believe in?\" closes Surah al-Mursalat with a final challenge after woe and not bowing. The question is rhetorical.\n\n“So what message after this Quran would they believe in?” translates the closing challenge, after winds sent, blowing, scattering, distinguishing, delivering to end excuses and give warnings, promised will come to pass, stars put out, sky torn, mountains blown, messengers timed, Day set, perfect ordainment, earth lodging, mountains and fresh water, smoke shade, sparks, silence, gathering, scheme, shade and springs, good-doers rewarded, little while for the wicked, bowing refused, and woe repeated. What message after this, or “fa-bi-ayyi hadithin ba‘dahu yu’minun,” what hadith, discourse after it will they believe? Hadith here is the Quran, the Reminder that would humble a mountain, the weighty revelation, the Pen and what everyone writes, the Light, the Balance, the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance.\n\nAfter this indicates that the Quran has covered winds, angels, creation, earth lodging, smoke, sparks, and Gardens, and if they do not believe this, no other message will convince, as with the despicable who said ancient fables and the elite who urged idols.\n\nThis follows woe to deniers who do not bow to show that their disbelief persists even after the most complete message.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think this invites seeking another message, like personal letters or unseen Record. It denies that; no other message after this will be more effective, as with the Reminder to the whole world.\n\nFor the living who are told this is a reminder so let whoever wills take the Right Way, believe in this message now, recite what is easy, establish prayer, pay alms, lend good loan, and seek forgiveness, so what message after this you believe in is this one, and your woe on that Day is not woe, but “All this is surely a reward, your striving appreciated,” and your vast kingdom and bliss remain."
};